<title>JAPAN: MOF says has already told DKB planned penalties.</title>
<headline>MOF says has already told DKB planned penalties.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) has already notified Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd (DKB) of punitive actions it plans to take against it for the bank's involvement in a racketeer payoff scandal, MOF sources said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The ministry was now waiting for the bank to express its views, one source said. He said the ministry would announce the measures against DKB on Wednesday if the bank had no objections to the penalties.</p>
<p>Other ministry sources said the announcement of the penalties was highly likely to be made in Wednesday afternoon.</p>
</text>
